# the stub allocates nothing: it writes the header and the word of the closure through the address in the frame that it is handed, and its row says that. What the closure captures lies in words that are written once, which no row names.
# Nor does a row name the word behind the captures, which the stub zeroes: it holds the address of the copy in the heap, and compiled code never reads it: only the run time does, where it moves the closure.
# RUN: emit f2 mechanisms=none+TypedOperations+Folding+EscapeAnalysis+CellsInFrames+DirectCalls
# CHECK-LABEL: unit f2:Body
# CHECK: = Patch({{*}}Writes:{ShapeWords
# PROGRAM-OF: ../walk/escape-analysis/direct-callee-marks-the-environment-that-it-keeps.ir
